== [check] What the new tab says, against these files
  OK   "Each VC3D release ... has two Windows downloads: `VC3D-*-win64.exe`, `VC3D-*-win64.zip`"
        26 of the 30 releases of ScrollPrize/villa are VC3D releases (named VC3D Latest or VC3D Stable); each
        publishes one VC3D-*-win64.exe and one VC3D-*-win64.zip.
  OK   "needs administrator rights"
        The installer asks Windows for requireAdministrator (see above), so Windows starts it only with
        administrator rights.
  OK   "VC3D is then in the Start menu"
        The installer creates the shortcut $SMPROGRAMS\$var33\VC3D.lnk to $INSTDIR\bin\VC3D.exe.
  OK   "by default `C:\Program Files\VC3D\bin` with the installer"
        InstallDir is $PROGRAMFILES\VC3D, C:\Program Files\VC3D here, and the programs go to $INSTDIR\bin.
  OK   "That folder is not added to `PATH`"
        The only code of the installer that writes PATH is one function, and its only call is always skipped
        (StrCmp "OFF" "ON").
  OK   "Both contain VC3D together with the `vc_*` command-line tools, in the `bin` folder"
        bin\ of the .zip: VC3D.exe and 19 vc_*.exe; $INSTDIR\bin of the installer: VC3D.exe and 17 vc_*.exe.
  OK   "There is nothing to install"
        The .zip holds no install program.
